# TEMPLATE. Copy to cluster.env and replace EVERY site value below with your own;
# cluster.env is gitignored and is the only place your site values live.
# The site-specific keys ship pre-filled with DUMMY data so the template is readable and
# self-consistent: the aliases gx10-a..gx10-d, the RFC 5737 documentation addresses
# 192.0.2.11..14 for the management LAN, the 10.10.<link>.<node> fabric plan and the login
# `alice`. They are NOT usable as-is: every script refuses to run while cluster.env still
# carries a `<...>` placeholder or the dummy NODES / MGMT_IPS / MASTER_IP / RELAY_DEST
# values (see scripts/lib/common.sh, scripts/tp4ctl and scripts/launcher/launch-glm53-tp4.sh).
# Everything that is NOT site-specific (image, model, window, scheduling, spec-decoding,
# the promoted EXTRA_* lines) is the production recipe of this repo: keep it as it is
# unless you are deliberately changing the lane.
# Immediate operational rollback:
# TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260930-e35.env removes only the E36 INT8 lm_head
# and returns to E35.
# TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260930-e31-mb.env removes E36 and the E35
# confidence-based verify length and returns to E31-MB.
# TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260929-memory-bounded.env removes E36, E35 and the
# SparkCache disk-capacity limit and returns to the 2026-09-29 memory-bounded recipe.
# TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260929-sparkcache-protected.env preserves
# the bounded SparkCache connector but restores the 16 GiB pool and removes allocator trim,
# the 6,912-token step cap, API admission and the disk-capacity limit. It is not the full
# memory-bounded recipe.
# Historical rollback TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/baseline-20260928-e31.env restores
# the measured E31 recipe and its previous unrestricted cache-memory behavior.
# Use it for deploy and all lifecycle commands after a coordinated stop with the serving
# recipe. Earlier complete returns are baseline-20260925-e29.env (the previous indexer),
# baseline-20260925-e28b.env (no end-drain), baseline-20260925-e27c.env (five draft tokens
# and a 15 GiB KV pool), baseline-20260924-e27.env (the image's scheduler),
# baseline-20260924-e22b.env (no prefill cadence) and
# baseline-20260923-e21.env (no E22b drafter conversion, the E21 cache namespace). The older
# E03 return is baseline-20260919-e03.env (the accepted E20 hook, no E21
# residue conversion, the E03 cache namespace); the pre-E03 base is baseline-20260919.env (hybrid
# KDA, previous scheduler and connector, 15 GiB KV); the September 18 rollback uses
# baseline-20260918.env and a 16 GiB pool.
# Preserve every source, payload and cache needed by those returns; see docs/operations.md.
# September 11 archive rollback: run `scripts/f0-reference.py plan-restore` against a
# verified private captured archive. That workflow stages the frozen controller and
# original base configuration; do not apply f0-20260912.env alone on this newer base.
# All measured baselines select GID -1, with the hardware-specific index-3 fallback
# documented beside NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX.
# cluster.env — the single recipe of this repo: GLM-5.3-Flash FP8 weights (zai-org)
# served on 4 nodes in TP4, with the DFlash2 drafter for speculative decoding
# (no in-card MTP).
# Sourced by: scripts/launcher/launch-glm53-tp4.sh, scripts/tp4ctl, scripts/deploy.sh and
# scripts/fetch-fp8-weights.sh.
# Every placeholder value is QUOTED so that this template is itself valid bash: `bash -n
# cluster.env.example` must pass (`scripts/check.sh` checks it), and `. cluster.env.example`
# in a subshell loads it with the placeholders as literal strings.
# Values containing $HOME are single-quoted on purpose: they must be expanded ON THE
# NODE, not on the workstation that runs scripts/tp4ctl. The launcher does that expansion itself,
# with plain parameter expansion and never `eval`: it covers MODEL_DIR, DRAFT_DIR,
# NCCL_DIR, PATCH_FILE, CACHE_DIR and the source of every `-v` pair in EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV.
# Drafter: incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 (base_model zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash = exactly the
# FP8 checkpoint served here; 5 layers, block_size 8, target_layer_ids [5,14,24,33,42],
# 2.34 GB bf16). License CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 (non-commercial; contact@inco.ai for commercial
# use). Install it as described in docs/install-from-zero.md.

# --- Topology: ssh aliases (from the workstation) and mgmt IPs in rank order 0..3 ---
# SITE VALUES — replace all four aliases and all four addresses.
# The alias of rank n must be the name you `ssh` the node with AND equal that node's
# `hostname -s` (scripts/deploy-host.sh refuses to install a netplan on a node whose
# hostname does not match its alias). See scripts/node/ssh-config.example.
NODES="gx10-a gx10-b gx10-c gx10-d"
MGMT_IPS="192.0.2.11 192.0.2.12 192.0.2.13 192.0.2.14"

# OPTIONAL. `hostname -s` of each node, in the same rank order. Default (empty or absent):
# the aliases of NODES. Set it only when the ssh alias and the host name differ — then
# scripts/deploy-host.sh checks the node's `hostname -s` against THIS list instead of the
# alias before installing that node's netplan. Same length as NODES.
NODE_HOSTNAMES="gx10-a gx10-b gx10-c gx10-d"

# --- Distributed rendez-vous and management network ---
# SITE VALUE: the management address of rank 0, i.e. the first entry of MGMT_IPS.
MASTER_IP="192.0.2.11"
# The rendez-vous port, the management interface name on the nodes and the API port are
# part of the recipe. The scalar is the verified homogeneous ASUS profile. If interface
# names differ between ranks, set the optional four-element array; it wins over MGMT_IF.
MASTER_PORT=29520
MGMT_IF=enP7s7
MGMT_IF_BY_RANK=()
# SECURITY: the launcher runs the container with `--network host` and vLLM binds
# 0.0.0.0:$API_PORT with NO authentication — no API key, no TLS, no allow-list. Anyone who
# can reach this port on the management LAN can use, and load, the endpoint. Run it on a
# TRUSTED LAN only; expose it further (reverse proxy with auth, VPN, firewall rule) before
# it is reachable from anywhere else.
API_PORT=8000

# --- Fabric ring topology, positional: the array index is the rank, and each entry
# holds the fabric IPs of that rank's two direct ring peers (8 directions in total).
# Used by scripts/tp4ctl fabric-check and by scripts/tp4ctl up.
# KEEP IN SYNC with the per-node netplan files under scripts/node/etc/ (see
# scripts/node/etc/40-cx7.yaml.example) and with RELAY_DEST below. Full map, cables and
# re-addressing checklist: docs/fabric.md.
# SITE VALUES, pre-filled with the RECOMMENDED plan: the address of node N on ring link L
# is 10.10.<L>.<N>/24, with L = 1..4 walking the ring rank0 -> rank1 -> rank2 -> rank3 ->
# rank0. Keep this plan and you only have to make scripts/node/etc/<alias>/40-cx7.yaml agree with
# it; use another plan and rewrite both. (Because it IS the recommended plan, this is the
# one site key the scripts do NOT reject for still holding the template value.)
FABRIC_TARGETS=(
  "10.10.1.2 10.10.4.4"
  "10.10.1.1 10.10.2.3"
  "10.10.2.2 10.10.3.4"
  "10.10.3.3 10.10.4.1"
)

# --- Fabric interface names, identical on every node, in netplan/iptables order:
# the first two are the ADDRESSED ports (f0, f1 — the two ends of this node's ring links),
# the last two are the second PCIe view of the same transceivers and carry MTU 9000 with no
# address. HARDWARE PROFILE, not a site value: these are the names verified on the ASUS
# Ascent GX10 (4x NVIDIA GB10). Different GB10 systems may name the same CX-7 ports
# differently — check `ip -br a` on a node and change all four, keeping the order.
# Consumers: scripts/render-netplan.sh (netplan plus the iptables interface environment)
# and scripts/verify-node.sh. For heterogeneous nodes, give exactly four quoted entries;
# an entry is the complete space-separated list for that rank and the array wins over the
# scalar. Empty array = use FABRIC_IFACES everywhere.
FABRIC_IFACES="enp1s0f0np0 enp1s0f1np1 enP2p1s0f0np0 enP2p1s0f1np1"
FABRIC_IFACES_BY_RANK=()

# RDMA device and RoCEv2 GID selection used by NCCL. These are the verified ASUS values.
# The HCA value is the comma-separated NCCL form. Per-rank arrays are optional but, when
# non-empty, must contain exactly four non-empty quoted entries. scripts/agent-preflight.sh
# proposes explicit values from sysfs discovery and blocks when the mapping is ambiguous.
# Optional NCCL automatic selection: set the scalar or a per-rank entry to -1. The launcher
# still fixes NCCL_IB_ADDR_FAMILY=AF_INET and NCCL_IB_ROCE_VERSION_NUM=2, and fails before
# Docker unless every selected active HCA port has an IPv4-mapped RoCEv2 GID whose netdev
# owns that address. Rollback: restore 3, or the previously verified non-negative per-rank
# entries. The September 19 baseline selects -1 (automatic per-HCA selection, as the frozen F0 overlay did); the
# launcher preflight and the SIRCL runtime both require the same IPv4 RoCEv2 GID per port.
# Rollback: 3, the verified explicit index of the F0 template.
NCCL_IB_HCA="rocep1s0f0,rocep1s0f1"
NCCL_IB_HCA_BY_RANK=()
NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=-1
NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX_BY_RANK=()

# Netplan renderer, homogeneous ASUS default or one value per rank. The renderer generates
# this into each node's 40-cx7.yaml; it is not guessed while deploying host assets.
NETPLAN_RENDERER=NetworkManager
NETPLAN_RENDERER_BY_RANK=()

# --- Rank-2 relay destination over the fabric, used by the weight fan-out of
# scripts/fetch-fp8-weights.sh: rank 2 has no direct link from the head, but rank 1 does,
# so its data leg can start from rank 1 over the direct rank1->rank2 link. See docs/fabric.md.
# SITE VALUE: <login on the nodes>@<rank 2's fabric address on the rank1<->rank2 link>.
RELAY_DEST='alice@10.10.2.3'

# --- Runtime ---
# Memory-bounded operational default, based on the accepted September 28 E31 recipe:
# docs/historical_benchmarks/baselines/2026-09-28-e31/baseline.json.
# The September 19 E03 recipe (R10 image, FP8, DFlash2, hybrid KDA, 15 GiB KV, mHC eager
# prefill sharding, replay views, draft-budget verification), plus E21: 8-bit weights for
# the residual BF16 attention projections (67 modules), plus E22b: 8-bit weights for 30
# DFlash2 drafter linears, with the drafter's fused context K/V projection kept in BF16,
# plus E27: the native prefill cadence, plus E27c: a scheduler that admits short prefills
# on deferred steps and keeps the cadence while requests are queued, plus E28b: seven draft
# tokens for a single request and a 16 GiB KV pool per rank.
# SparkCache adds 8 MiB disk-transfer chunks, a shared 1 GiB transient budget per rank
# and a 1 GiB MemAvailable admission floor. The operational layer adds a 14 GiB KV pool,
# eager-prefill allocator trim, a 6,912-token per-step scheduler cap and finite API
# admission (6 active plus 128 queued), and SparkCache keeps at most 200 GiB on disk per
# rank. E35 lets the model runner verify 3 or 7 drafts of a single-request decode step from
# the drafter's own confidence (policy hybrid), and E36 packs the shared lm_head in INT8.
# Immediate operational rollbacks: TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260930-e35.env
# (no E36), then TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260930-e31-mb.env (no E36, no E35),
# then TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260929-memory-bounded.env (no E36, no E35, no
# disk limit), then TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260929-sparkcache-protected.env.
# Historical E31 rollback remains scripts/node/reference/baseline-20260928-e31.env.
# The native SIRCL entrypoint uses /health; --no-healthcheck remains intentional.
# Historical F0 rollback lane, for reference only; it is not an active setting:
# IMAGE=ghcr.io/tonyd2wild/vllm-glm53-flash:sm121-v11-dflash2,
# IMAGE_ID="", SPARKCACHE_MODE=off and the older values named below. The archived
# reference workflow is documented in docs/operations.md.
IMAGE=ghcr.io/fujitsupolycom/sparkring-glm53-sparkcache@sha256:0d4029b3b7023cf32c37ac20279469c9a2ee16a057f25aae3bcfee9ee5fb660f
IMAGE_ID=sha256:5e32aaa1bbe3559e81db7706ed4286248f18d27cfdb186f6b851bf786eb43075
CONTAINER=glm53_fp8_dflash_tp4
# --- Launcher invoked by tp4ctl on every node (~/tp4/$LAUNCHER) ---
LAUNCHER=launch-glm53-tp4.sh

# --- SparkCache persistent prefix cache ---
# SPARKCACHE_MODE=on makes the launcher own --kv-transfer-config, verify the config and the
# connector and encoder overrides against the SHA-256 pins below, skip the PATCH_FILE mount
# (the R10 image carries the indexer patch) and verify the SIRCL payload. Configs are
# managed under scripts/node/ and deployed with the same relative layout below ~/tp4/. The
# Apache-2.0 connector, encoder and SIRCL bundle/runtime are included under third_party/
# (docs/third-party.md); scripts/deploy.sh places them under ~/tp4/sparkcache/ and
# ~/tp4/sircl/, and the deployed SHA256SUMS in those directories are the only accepted
# identities. The SIRCL per-rank files are site data: generate them with
# scripts/sircl-site-files.sh (docs/install-from-zero.md). Leave SPARKCACHE_CONNECTOR or
# SPARKCACHE_ENCODER empty only when deliberately selecting the corresponding image module.
# The measured E31 rollback retains the E22b namespace. This protected default uses a new
# cpu-budget namespace; E21 and E03 keep their own namespaces because converted weights,
# drafter state and mHC reduction order affect the cached representation.
# Rollback: use a complete reference overlay; do not mix payload versions.
SPARKCACHE_MODE=on
# The protected connector transfers snapshot data through disk in 8 MiB pieces. Its
# config admits at most 1 GiB of shared transient cache work per rank and requires 1 GiB
# of remaining MemAvailable. Pressure skips a store or recomputes a rejected restore.
# Historical cache-behavior rollback: use baseline-20260928-e31.env; it restores the
# previous connector, config and cache namespace while retaining the measured E31 engine.
SPARKCACHE_CONFIG='$HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/sparkcache-ram-budget/kv-transfer-config.json'
SPARKCACHE_CONFIG_SHA256=d99bd6720572b2f46668d0a11229f7662f1e8fdd69a69f61cbfa5592aa600c72
SPARKCACHE_CONNECTOR='$HOME/tp4/sparkcache/spark_context_cache_connector-ram-budget.py'
SPARKCACHE_CONNECTOR_SHA256=aa046965637b685ec1f6a00e427eb46279e28bf0d49ee546236bc774be2de9bd
SPARKCACHE_ENCODER='$HOME/tp4/sparkcache/spark_context_cache_hybrid.py'
SPARKCACHE_ENCODER_SHA256=11a2db855306b816a4f3d377d04207cc2d62112a381bcc54162099248bbf75f6
SIRCL_DIR='$HOME/tp4/sircl'

# --- Paths on the nodes (expanded at runtime, on the node) ---
# Flat layout: MODEL_DIR is the directory of the zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash card downloaded
# with scripts/fetch-fp8-weights.sh (~306 GiB, 62 shards model-*-of-00062) and mounted
# whole as /model:ro (no hub/models--*/blobs indirection).
MODEL_DIR='$HOME/glm53-flash-fp8-zai'
MODEL_REPO=zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash
# MODEL_REV / DRAFT_REV: the reproducibility pin of a release — the HF commit sha of the
# checkpoint, i.e. what `hf download --revision` fetches and what the first line of
# <dir>/.cache/huggingface/download/config.json.metadata records on the node that ran the
# download. Empty = follow the card's HEAD, and then the effective identity is the
# fingerprint scripts/verify-node.sh prints (sha256 of config.json + shard count).
# The values below are PUBLIC information (upstream commits), not site values: they are the
# ones this recipe uses, verified on the nodes on 2026-09-04.
#   MODEL_REV  read by scripts/fetch-fp8-weights.sh (`hf download --revision`) and written
#              into the .glm53-fp8-synced fan-out marker; compared by verify-node.sh.
#   DRAFT_REV  the DFlash2 drafter is fetched separately (docs/install-from-zero.md), so no script
#              downloads it; verify-node.sh compares it with the drafter's own metadata.
# 2026-09-04 template/tool-call fix. Rollback: restore the prior manifest revision
# 03eb5366286afd40d2221b1d9c63a6dd1ba4832e, fetch it, deploy, then restart full TP4.
MODEL_REV="690b705278a3a58e538fcb37c2ca8b5f9511213c"
DRAFT_DIR='$HOME/glm53-dflash2-draft'
DRAFT_REV="bf582e4eacc1810f76656d1811693ff6c6737d2a"
# sm121 indexer patch for the F0 image (v11). With SPARKCACHE_MODE=on the R10 image
# carries the patch and the launcher does not mount this file; keep it for the rollback lane.
# Fallbacks are documented at the top of the launcher.
PATCH_FILE='$HOME/patches/sparse_attn_indexer_kpool.py'
NCCL_DIR='$HOME/nccl-patched'
# CACHE_DIR must be disk-backed, not tmpfs, with room for the persistent cache plus at least
# one in-flight SparkCache snapshot staging file.
CACHE_DIR='$HOME/vllm-cache'

# --- Identity of the served model ---
SERVED_NAME=glm-5.3-flash

# --- Context window and KV cache ---
# Maximum context 262144, up to six scheduled sequences. The launcher
# adds VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1 only above 262144, so it is no longer injected.
# The historical C5 functionality overlays under scripts/node/experiments/e03-c5/ apply
# only to the E03 base and refuse the current default, because they pin the E03 SparkCache
# config. They were never measured for performance with the current default.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
MAX_NUM_SEQS=6
# Explicit 14 GiB per rank in EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS: with seven draft tokens the engine reports
# 1,194,033 KV tokens, about 4.55 full 262144-token windows. MAX_NUM_SEQS=6 and six active
# API admission slots do not promise six resident full windows; five full contexts require
# waiting or preemption. The protected operational rollback above restores 16 GiB. E27c and
# earlier used 15 GiB (1,344,328 tokens with five draft tokens).
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8_e4m3

# --- Scheduling / batching ---
BATCHED_TOKENS=8192
# Default E03 mHC path: exactly 6,912 eager target rows, 1,728 rows per TP rank.
# Sources retain their measured experiments/e03 paths and SHA-256 identities.
# Its dedicated SparkCache namespace must remain separate from the previous base.
# Rollback all coupled source/config changes with baseline-20260919.env.
SPARK_MHC_PREFILL_SHARD=1
BLOCK_SIZE=2304
# Rank 0 also hosts the API process: 0.89+ means NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY on the head
# (0.885 works only with the GUI stripped from the OS).
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85

# --- Speculative decoding (DFlash2 drafter, no in-card MTP) ---
# The drafter block size is 8. E28 supplies seven draft tokens for one request and
# three for batches of 2–6 (E27c and earlier: five and three). VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_HI=7 in
# EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV lets the adaptive high state use all seven; the low state stays three.
# Seven tokens hold about 4.9% fewer KV tokens per GiB, so E28b also raises the pool to
# 16 GiB (see KV_CACHE_DTYPE). baseline-20260925-e27c.env restores five tokens and 15 GiB as
# one return. The measured scheduler caps its adaptive placeholders
# using the same SchedulerOutput budget consumed by the worker, preserving async
# observations and batch-uniform graphs. VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_RESPECT_DRAFT_BUDGET=1
# is coupled to its mount in EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV. The prior scheduler source and hash
# remain intact for baseline-20260919.env; changing only this flag is not a full rollback.
# Rollback of the adaptive scheduler (one step): SPEC_TOKENS=3, SPEC_EXTRA_JSON="",
# remove --scheduler-cls from EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS and the /opt/tp4 mount + VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_* from
# EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV as one coupled edit, deploy, restart.
SPEC_TOKENS=7
# Extra JSON inside --speculative-config: the dynamic-speculation table makes the runner capture
# FULL decode CUDA graphs for both verify sizes (k=3 -> 4 tokens, k=7 -> 8 tokens); on the async
# scheduler path it would also set k by batch size, which the AdaptiveKScheduler overrides per request.
# The R10 recipe also pins the drafter's KV dtype: the R10 target B12X normalization must not flow
# fp8_ds_mla into the Qwen3 DFlash2 cache. Rollback (F0 lane): drop the kv_cache_dtype pair.
SPEC_EXTRA_JSON='"num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size":[[1,1,7],[2,6,3]],"kv_cache_dtype":"fp8_e4m3"'
# 0 = omit --async-scheduling; 1 forces it on. With the current compatible DFlash2/MP
# recipe, omission lets vLLM resolve async scheduling on automatically. The startup log
# must still report AdaptiveKScheduler enabled=1 and async=True.
ASYNC_SCHEDULING=0

# --- Extra docker run arguments, inserted right after the fixed env block ---
# Free-form list of arguments handed to `docker run` before the image name: `-e VAR=val`,
# `-v /host:/ctr:ro`, `--cpuset-cpus 0-9`, ... It is word-split on spaces, so no value may
# contain a space, and no glob characters (* ?): the value is word-split AND
# pathname-expanded. The launcher rejects NCCL_IB_HCA, NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX,
# NCCL_IB_ROCE_VERSION_NUM, NCCL_IB_ADDR_FAMILY, or NCCL_IB_ADDR_RANGE in `-e`, `--env`,
# or an environment file here, then reapplies the four validated selector values after
# this string. A TP4_ENV delta is the supported place to change HCA/GID selection; see
# docs/operations.md.
#
# Non-empty in production since 2026-09-04: it mounts the selected GB10 Triton fused-MoE
# kernel config over the one the image ships. The file contains platform-specific entries
# for batch sizes 1, 2, 4, and 8, plus vLLM's own `get_default_config()` values for 16-48
# and 1024-8192, so every other size keeps the upstream default behavior.
#
# The JSON is versioned under scripts/node/moe-configs/ and scripts/deploy.sh pushes it to
# ~/tp4/moe-configs/ on all nodes. The value is SINGLE-quoted and the mount sources are
# written as $HOME/...: the launcher expands a leading $HOME (or ~) in the source of every
# `-v` pair, on the node, before word-splitting them into the docker argv. The name carries
# commas, '=' and '[]' but no spaces, so the word-splitting is safe and the glob-looking
# `[128,128]` matches nothing on disk. If the file is missing on a node, `docker run` would create a
# DIRECTORY at the mount target and the rank would boot on a broken configs dir: the
# launcher preflight checks every `-v` source in EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV and aborts the rank first.
# Rollback: remove only the MoE JSON mount from EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV (preserve the scheduler
# mount and policy variables), then ./scripts/deploy.sh + ./scripts/tp4ctl restart.
#
# The September 18 recipe introduced these coupled components:
#  * VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_MODE=batch-uniform: one verify length per step (k_hi only when every
#    placeholder request is in the high state), so a step never mixes k=3 and k=5 and the
#    target always runs the FULL decode graph. Qualified 2026-09-18 (C4 +18.2%, C2 within
#    noise vs F0). Rollback: per-request.
#  * six original vLLM override mounts from scripts/node/overrides/ (deployed to ~/tp4/overrides/):
#    the R10 KV-cache interface/utils/worker split for the dense DFlash draft allocation, the
#    pooled-indexer tail correction (glm_kpool), the legacy checkpoint-exclusion mapper
#    (model.py) and the physical-selection contract (pooled_indexer). Rollback: drop the six
#    -v pairs together with the R10 image.
#  * the SIRCL single-rail sync-prefill transport: bundle at /opt/spark-sircl, runtime at
#    /opt/sircl-serving and its entrypoint, which sources the per-rank env files and verifies
#    its own SHA256SUMS. Rollback: drop the two -v pairs and --entrypoint together with the
#    R10 image (the F0 image uses its default entrypoint).
#  * the reviewed connector override at the image path (exactly once; the launcher checks).
#    For a complete rollback, use the frozen overlay rather than mixing connector versions.
# September 19 also mounts e20_kda_w8a16.py, e20_hybrid_scratch.py and gpu_worker.py.
# model.py converts 34 KDA input projections to group-128 INT8 at load time. Below
# 2048 flattened input rows it uses Marlin; at/above 2048 it dequantizes into one shared
# BF16 scratch buffer and calls the dense GEMM. The worker retains the measured
# non-synchronizing memory probe. The cache encoder avoids a duplicate bytes allocation.
# Technical module names are retained to preserve measured source identities. Rollback
# all of these with baseline-20260918.env, including model.py and the cache namespace.
# The accepted E03 recipe additionally replaces model.py and mounts eight mHC modules;
# its replay connector and draft-budget scheduler retain their measured paths/hashes.
# baseline-20260919.env removes those three accepted deltas as one complete return.
# The accepted E21 recipe replaces the e20_kda_w8a16.py mount with the bf16-residue copy
# (the accepted source plus one flag-gated call), mounts e21_bf16_residue.py and sets
# VLLM_E21_BF16_RESIDUE_W8A16=1. It converts 67 more BF16 projections to 8-bit weights and
# logs E21_BF16_RESIDUE_W8A16_READY. baseline-20260919-e03.env removes it as one return.
# The accepted E22b recipe mounts the drafter override qwen3_dflash2.py (the image's file
# plus one appended, flag-gated load hook) and e22_drafter_w8a16.py, and sets
# VLLM_E22_DRAFTER_W8A16=1 with VLLM_E22_CONTEXT_KV_W8A16=0. It converts 30 drafter
# linears to 8-bit weights, keeps the context K/V projection in BF16 and logs
# E22_DRAFTER_W8A16_READY with 30 modules. baseline-20260923-e21.env removes it as one return.
# The accepted E27c recipe mounts experiments/e03/queued-cadence/scheduler.py over the
# image's scheduler (the image's file plus one reviewed patch of its prefill-deferral gates)
# and sets VLLM_E27B_SHORT_PREFILL_TOKENS=2048 and VLLM_E27C_CADENCE_WHEN_QUEUED=1. With the
# E27 cadence, a deferred step still admits prefills with fewer than 2,048 remaining tokens
# (up to 2,048 per step), and the cadence stays on while requests are queued. It logs
# E27C_CADENCE_WHEN_QUEUED_READY and E27B_SHORT_PREFILL_READY tokens=2048 interval=8.
# baseline-20260924-e27.env removes it as one return.
# The accepted E29 recipe mounts experiments/e03/end-drain/scheduler.py instead (the E27c
# scheduler plus one additions-only patch) and the image's engine core with one
# additions-only patch (experiments/e03/end-drain/core.py), and sets VLLM_E29_END_DRAIN=1,
# VLLM_E29_IDLE_COALESCE_MS=4 and VLLM_E29_TRACE=0. With asynchronous scheduling a request
# limited by max_tokens is not given another speculative step while the step in flight may
# finish it, so the next request no longer waits behind a useless verification step; at an
# idle engine, requests arriving within 4 ms are prefilled in one step. It logs
# E29_END_DRAIN_READY trace=0 and E29_IDLE_COALESCE_READY ms=4 trace=0.
# baseline-20260925-e28b.env removes it as one return.
# The accepted E31 recipe mounts experiments/e03/e31-indexer/pooled_indexer.py and
# experiments/e03/e31-indexer/glm_kpool.py instead of the two production indexer overrides,
# and names the in-container flag files VLLM_GLM53_INDEXER_GATE_TC_FLAG and
# VLLM_GLM53_KPOOL_TAIL_RING_FLAG. The C4 key/gate tail becomes a ring of 4 * cdiv(4 + K, 4)
# slots (12 for seven drafts), so the rows of a DFlash verify step, including rejected
# drafts, no longer overwrite committed members of the still-open pool. The switch defaults
# stay as measured: head gate on FP32 (VLLM_GLM53_INDEXER_GATE_TC unset = 0) and the ring on
# (VLLM_GLM53_KPOOL_TAIL_RING unset = 1). It logs E31_INDEXER_GATE path=fp32 and
# E31_KPOOL_TAIL_RING ring=12. baseline-20260925-e29.env removes it as one return.
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV='-v $HOME/tp4/moe-configs/E=288,N=512,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/configs/E=288,N=512,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,dtype=fp8_w8a8,block_shape=[128,128].json:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/draft-budget/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:/opt/tp4/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:ro -e PYTHONPATH=/opt/tp4 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_MODE=batch-uniform -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_SEED=1.0 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_DOWN=0.42 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_UP=0.58 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_ALPHA=0.15 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_SIGNAL=pos -v $HOME/tp4/overrides/vllm/v1/kv_cache_interface.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/kv_cache_interface.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/overrides/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/overrides/vllm/v1/worker/utils.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/worker/utils.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/e31-indexer/glm_kpool.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/ops/glm_kpool.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/e31-indexer/pooled_indexer.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/pooled_indexer.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/sircl/bundle:/opt/spark-sircl:ro -v $HOME/tp4/sircl/runtime:/opt/sircl-serving:ro --entrypoint /opt/sircl-serving/entrypoint.sh -v $HOME/tp4/sparkcache/spark_context_cache_connector-e03-replay-views.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/sparkcache/spark_context_cache_connector.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/bf16-residue/e20_kda_w8a16.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/e20_kda_w8a16.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/overrides/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/e20_hybrid_scratch.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/e20_hybrid_scratch.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/sparkcache/spark_context_cache_hybrid.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/sparkcache/spark_context_cache_hybrid.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/prefill-cache-trim/gpu_worker.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/runner/moe_runner.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/runner/moe_runner.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/runner/moe_runner_interface.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/runner/moe_runner_interface.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/model_executor/layers/linear.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/linear.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/kimi_gdn_linear_attn.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/mamba/gdn/kimi_gdn_linear_attn.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/model_executor/layers/mla.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/layers/mla.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/attention.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/attention.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/kda.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/kda.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/mhc_prefill_sharding.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/mhc_prefill_sharding.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/overrides/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/model.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/model.py:ro -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_RESPECT_DRAFT_BUDGET=1 -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/bf16-residue/e21_bf16_residue.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/e21_bf16_residue.py:ro -e VLLM_E21_BF16_RESIDUE_W8A16=1 -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/drafter-w8a16/qwen3_dflash2.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_dflash2.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/drafter-w8a16/e22_drafter_w8a16.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/e22_drafter_w8a16.py:ro -e VLLM_E22_DRAFTER_W8A16=1 -e VLLM_E22_CONTEXT_KV_W8A16=0 -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/prefill-step-cap/scheduler.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py:ro -e VLLM_E27B_SHORT_PREFILL_TOKENS=2048 -e VLLM_E27C_CADENCE_WHEN_QUEUED=1 -e VLLM_ADAPTIVE_K_HI=7 -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/end-drain/core.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/engine/core.py:ro -e VLLM_E29_END_DRAIN=1 -e VLLM_E29_IDLE_COALESCE_MS=4 -e VLLM_E29_TRACE=0 -e VLLM_GLM53_INDEXER_GATE_TC_FLAG=/tmp/glm53-indexer-gate-tc -e VLLM_GLM53_KPOOL_TAIL_RING_FLAG=/tmp/glm53-kpool-tail-ring -e VLLM_PREFILL_CACHE_TRIM=1 -e VLLM_RESILIENCE_STEP_TOKEN_CAP=6912 -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/bounded-admission/middleware.py:/opt/tp4/tp4_admission.py:ro -e TP4_ADMISSION_MAX_ACTIVE=6 -e TP4_ADMISSION_MAX_QUEUED=128 -e TP4_ADMISSION_MAX_BODY_BYTES=8388608 -e TP4_ADMISSION_QUEUE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800 -e TP4_ADMISSION_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600 -e TP4_ADMISSION_BODY_IDLE_SECONDS=30 -e TP4_ADMISSION_SEND_IDLE_SECONDS=30'

# --- Extra vLLM arguments, appended last ---
# --moe-backend triton selects the backend used with the mounted GB10 configuration.
# Without the explicit selection, vLLM's `triton_deep_gemm_moe` chooses DeepGEMM E8M0
# for every M because the upstream `N <= 512 -> Triton` fast path does not fire at
# N=512 per rank under TP4. Dense FP8 linears stay on DeepGEMM E8M0; attention is unchanged.
# Rollback: drop --moe-backend triton (DeepGEMM auto-select) and its tuned JSON mount.
# R10 engine: the KV pool flag is spelled --kv-cache-memory-bytes, and the attention
# and dense-linear backends are selected explicitly (B12X, Triton). --kv-transfer-config is
# added by the launcher (never here). Rollback (F0 lane):
# EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS="--kv-cache-memory=17179869184 --moe-backend triton --scheduler-cls adaptive_k_scheduler.AdaptiveKScheduler"
# The operational 14 GiB pool is 12.5% smaller than E31's measured 16 GiB pool.
# Startup reports 1,194,033 KV tokens (4.55 x 262,144), so five complete
# maximum-length contexts cannot be resident at once and must queue.
# The accepted E27 recipe adds the image's native --prefill-schedule-interval 8.
# - While requests decode, prefill work runs on one engine step in eight; the steps in
#   between are decode-only. Running requests therefore keep generating while another
#   client cold-prefills a long context.
# - A prefill with no running decode is not deferred. With the image's scheduler alone, the
#   cadence stops while requests are queued; the E27c scheduler mounted above keeps it on and
#   lets short prefills through.
# - Cost: time to first token for long prompts that arrive while others decode.
# - baseline-20260924-e22b.env removes the cadence and the E27c scheduler as one return.
# --compilation-config={"max_cudagraph_capture_size":72} keeps the E27c CUDA graph set with seven
# draft tokens; without it vLLM would capture up to 96 and use more memory on rank 0.
# Select the protected connector in the single existing mount. Keeping the substitution
# adjacent to the complete mount list makes the one-file rollback above reviewable.
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV=${EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV/spark_context_cache_connector-e03-replay-views.py/spark_context_cache_connector-ram-budget.py}
# SparkCache disk capacity per rank (operational policy, not a performance setting). Without
# a limit the store grows until the root filesystem is full; stores then fail and long
# replays recompute. Once its accounted files exceed 200 GiB, the connector removes the
# approximately least recently used entries until 160 GiB remain; each rank's worker scans
# its store at startup. Transient spool files are not counted, so size both values with
# headroom below the disk left after weights, image and logs. The connector reads these variables only while
# its JSON config leaves the keys unset. Rollback to an unlimited store (it also removes E36/E35):
# TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260929-memory-bounded.env.
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV+=" -e SPARK_CONTEXT_CACHE_MAX_BYTES=214748364800 -e SPARK_CONTEXT_CACHE_LOW_WATERMARK_BYTES=171798691840"
# E35 verify length from the drafter's confidence (promoted 2026-09-30). On a decode step with
# one request and seven scheduled drafts, rank 0 of the V2 model runner chooses to verify 3 or
# 7 drafts from the DFlash2 selector's per-position confidence and broadcasts the choice to
# every tensor-parallel rank; trimmed drafts count as rejected. The scheduler copy gives such
# steps seven drafts while the policy is lag1 or hybrid. The read-only policy file selects
# hybrid (wait for the current draft only on uncertain steps). Rank 0 re-reads it every
# 0.5 s: overwriting the host file on rank 0 in place with `ema` restores the acceptance-EMA
# length without a restart until the next deploy. Rollback to E31-MB (it also removes E36):
# TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260930-e31-mb.env.
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV=${EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV/draft-budget\/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:/e35-runner-k/adaptive_k_scheduler.py:}
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV+=' -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/e35-runner-k/model_runner.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py:ro -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/e35-runner-k/speculator.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash2/speculator.py:ro -e VLLM_E35_ENABLE=1 -e VLLM_E35_POLICY_FLAG=/tmp/glm53-e35-policy -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/e35-runner-k/policy.flag:/tmp/glm53-e35-policy:ro'
# E36 INT8 lm_head (promoted 2026-09-30). The vocab-parallel lm_head that the target shares with
# the DFlash2 drafter becomes INT8 W8A16 (symmetric, group 128, Marlin) once both models load,
# before CUDA graphs are captured; the BF16 head is freed (about 155 MB per rank net). The E36
# runner is the E35 runner plus that load-time conversion. Target logits change slightly (dense
# perplexity +0.018% in the fidelity measurement); the SparkCache namespace does not. One-step
# rollback to E35: TP4_ENV=scripts/node/reference/operational-20260930-e35.env.
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV=${EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV/e35-runner-k\/model_runner.py:/e36-lm-head-w8a16/model_runner.py:}
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV+=' -v $HOME/tp4/experiments/e03/e36-lm-head-w8a16/e36_lm_head_w8a16.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/glm5next/nvidia/e36_lm_head_w8a16.py:ro -e VLLM_E36_LM_HEAD_W8A16=1 -e VLLM_E36_KEEP_BF16=0'
EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS="--kv-cache-memory-bytes=15032385536 --attention-backend B12X --moe-backend triton --linear-backend triton --scheduler-cls adaptive_k_scheduler.AdaptiveKScheduler --prefill-schedule-interval 8 --compilation-config={\"max_cudagraph_capture_size\":72} --middleware tp4_admission.BoundedAdmissionMiddleware"
